maya: Heads-up — hit a reproducible bug when running the JS SDK in Bun/Deno edge mode: Authorization header is missing on the retry after a 401.

sam: Can you paste a tiny repro?

maya: Yep. Importing ESM in Deno via import_map, but Bun sometimes resolves to our CJS shim. Flow: initial fetch -> 401 -> refresh token -> mutate opts.headers and fetch again. Second request reaches server with no Authorization.

maya: Minimal retry helper:```js
async function doRequest(url, opts){
  const res = await fetch(url, opts);
  if(res.status === 401){
    const token = await refresh();
    opts.headers = { ...opts.headers, Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }
    return fetch(url, opts) // observed missing header in Bun/Deno
  }
  return res
}
```

jonah: Which runtimes/versions?

maya: Bun 1.1.x and Deno 1.35 (our edge test harness). Server logs show header omitted on retry. Bun's inspector also shows no Authorization on second call.

li: Likely root cause: some runtimes consume or otherwise finalize Headers/Request when used. Always safe to create fresh Headers or Request for retry:```js
const headers = new Headers(opts.headers || {});
headers.set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`);
return fetch(url, { ...opts, headers })
```

sam: Also our Bun shim did `globalThis.fetch = (p,o) => nativeFetch(new Request(p,o))` which can eat streams/headers. Switching to `nativeFetch(p, { ...o, headers: new Headers(o?.headers) })` is more robust.

maya: I implemented a tiny cross-build util cloneHeaders() and wired retry paths to use it. Fixes the repro locally.

ci-bot: Created issue RED-DEVEX-472 and opened PR https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/839 (adds header clone util + tests for Bun/Deno).

sam: Nice. Add an integration test that runs the repro under Bun and Deno (optional CI matrix). Also export the util from ESM entry so conditional exports don't duplicate logic.

maya: Will do, plus a short changelog note under "compatibility fixes". Ping for review @sam.

jonah: Thanks for the quick repro — saved a lot of time.
